expandable-expanded\" style=\"\"><div class=\"wprm-internal-container-toggle\"><a role=\"button\" aria-expanded=\"false\" class=\"wprm-expandable-button wprm-expandable-button-show\" aria-label=\"Show Section\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-icon wprm-collapsible-icon\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\"><g class=\"nc-icon-wrapper\" stroke-width=\"1\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#333333\" stroke-miterlimit=\"10\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"><polyline points=\"3.5,9.5 8,5 12.5,9.5 \"></polyline></g></svg></span> </a><a role=\"button\" aria-expanded=\"true\" class=\"wprm-expandable-button wprm-expandable-button-hide\" aria-label=\"Hide Section\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-icon wprm-collapsible-icon\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\"><g class=\"nc-icon-wrapper\" stroke-width=\"1\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#333333\" stroke-miterlimit=\"10\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"><polyline points=\"3.5,6.5 8,11 12.5,6.5 \"></polyline></g></svg></span> </a></div><div class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-group\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-group-name wprm-recipe-ingredient-group-name wprm-block-text-bold\" style=\"color: var(--meadow-accent-color);\">Base Ingredients</div><div class=\"wprm-spacer\" style=\"height: 5px;\"></div><ul class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredients\"><li class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient\" style=\"list-style-type: none;border-bottom: 1px solid var(--meadow-list-border-color);padding-bottom: 5px;margin-bottom: 5px;\" data-uid=\"-1\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount\">1</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit\">can (10 oz)</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-name\">Rotel diced tomatoes and green chilies</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes-faded\">For a zesty base.</span></li><li class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient\" style=\"list-style-type: none;border-bottom: 1px solid var(--meadow-list-border-color);padding-bottom: 5px;margin-bottom: 5px;\" data-uid=\"-1\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount\">1</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit\">lb</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-name\">Velveeta cheese</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes-faded\">Cubed for smooth melting.</span></li><li class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient\" style=\"list-style-type: none;\" data-uid=\"-1\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount\">1</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit\">lb</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-name\">Ground beef</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes-faded\">Provides that hearty flavor.</span></li></ul></div><div class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-group\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-group-name wprm-recipe-ingredient-group-name wprm-block-text-bold\" style=\"color: var(--meadow-accent-color);\">Vegetables</div><div class=\"wprm-spacer\" style=\"height: 5px;\"></div><ul class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredients\"><li class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient\" style=\"list-style-type: none;border-bottom: 1px solid var(--meadow-list-border-color);padding-bottom: 5px;margin-bottom: 5px;\" data-uid=\"-1\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount\">1</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit\">small</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-name\">Onion</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes-faded\">Finely chopped for sweetness.</span></li><li class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient\" style=\"list-style-type: none;border-bottom: 1px solid var(--meadow-list-border-color);padding-bottom: 5px;margin-bottom: 5px;\" data-uid=\"-1\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount\">2</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit\">cloves</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-name\">Garlic</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes-faded\">Minced for a punch of flavor.</span></li><li class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient\" style=\"list-style-type: none;\" data-uid=\"-1\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount\">1</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit\">tsp</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-name\">Chili powder</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes-faded\">Optional for extra spice if desired.</span></li></ul></div><div class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-group\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-group-name wprm-recipe-ingredient-group-name wprm-block-text-bold\" style=\"color: var(--meadow-accent-color);\">Garnish</div><div class=\"wprm-spacer\" style=\"height: 5px;\"></div><ul class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredients\"><li class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient\" style=\"list-style-type: none;\" data-uid=\"-1\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount\">to taste</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-name\">Fresh cilantro or green onions</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes-faded\">For garnish.</span></li></ul></div></div></div>\n      <div id=\"recipe-5129-equipment\" class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-container wprm-block-text-normal\" data-recipe=\"5129\"><h3 class=\"wprm-recipe-header wprm-recipe-equipment-header wprm-block-text-bold wprm-align-left wprm-header-decoration-none\" style=\"\">Equipment</h3><div class=\"wprm-spacer\" style=\"height: 15px;\"></div><div class=\"wprm-internal-container wprm-internal-container-equipment wprm-expandable-container wprm-expandable-expanded\" style=\"\"><div class=\"wprm-internal-container-toggle\"><a role=\"button\" aria-expanded=\"false\" class=\"wprm-expandable-button wprm-expandable-button-show\" aria-label=\"Show Section\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-icon wprm-collapsible-icon\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\"><g class=\"nc-icon-wrapper\" stroke-width=\"1\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#333333\" stroke-miterlimit=\"10\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"><polyline points=\"3.5,9.5 8,5 12.5,9.5 \"></polyline></g></svg></span> </a><a role=\"button\" aria-expanded=\"true\" class=\"wprm-expandable-button wprm-expandable-button-hide\" aria-label=\"Hide Section\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-icon wprm-collapsible-icon\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\"><g class=\"nc-icon-wrapper\" stroke-width=\"1\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#333333\" stroke-miterlimit=\"10\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"><polyline points=\"3.5,6.5 8,11 12.5,6.5 \"></polyline></g></svg></span> </a></div><ul class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment wprm-recipe-equipment-list\"><li class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-item\" style=\"list-style-type: none;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-name\">1 Skillet&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-notes wprm-recipe-equipment-notes-normal\">For browning the beef and melting the cheese.</span></div></li></ul></div></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"wprm-layout-column wprm-column-width-50 meadow-main-right\">\n      <div id=\"recipe-5129-instructions\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instructions-container wprm-recipe-5129-instructions-container wprm-block-text-normal\" data-recipe=\"5129\"><h3 class=\"wprm-recipe-header wprm-recipe-instructions-header wprm-block-text-bold wprm-align-left wprm-header-decoration-spacer wprm-header-has-actions\" style=\"\">Method<div class=\"wprm-decoration-spacer\"></div>&nbsp;</h3><div class=\"wprm-spacer\" style=\"height: 15px;\"></div><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-group\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-group-name wprm-recipe-instruction-group-name wprm-block-text-bold\" style=\"color: #000000;\">Cooking Steps</div><div class=\"wprm-spacer\" style=\"height: 5px;\"></div><ol class=\"wprm-recipe-instructions\"><li id=\"wprm-recipe-5129-step-0-0\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction\" style=\"list-style-type: decimal;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-text\" style=\"margin-bottom: 10px;\"><span style=\"display: block;\">Step 1: In a skillet over medium heat, brown the ground beef until no longer pink. Drain any excess fat.</span></div></li><li id=\"wprm-recipe-5129-step-0-1\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction\" style=\"list-style-type: decimal;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-text\" style=\"margin-bottom: 10px;\"><span style=\"display: block;\">Step 2: Add chopped onion and minced garlic to the skillet. Sauté until softened, about 3–4 minutes.</span></div></li><li id=\"wprm-recipe-5129-step-0-2\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction\" style=\"list-style-type: decimal;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-text\" style=\"margin-bottom: 10px;\"><span style=\"display: block;\">Step 3: Reduce heat to low. Add cubed Velveeta and the can of Rotel (undrained). Stir continuously until the cheese is fully melted and the mixture is smooth.</span></div></li><li id=\"wprm-recipe-5129-step-0-3\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction\" style=\"list-style-type: decimal;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-text\" style=\"margin-bottom: 10px;\"><span style=\"display: block;\">Step 4: Season with chili powder if desired. Stir to combine all the flavors.</span></div></li><li id=\"wprm-recipe-5129-step-0-4\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction\" style=\"list-style-type: decimal;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-text\" style=\"margin-bottom: 10px;\"><span style=\"display: block;\">Step 5: Transfer to a serving bowl. Garnish with cilantro or green onions. Serve warm with tortilla chips.</span></div></li></ol></div></div>\n      \n      <div id=\"recipe-video\"></div>\n      <div id=\"recipe-5129-notes\" class=\"wprm-recipe-notes-container wprm-block-text-normal\"><h3 class=\"wprm-recipe-header wprm-recipe-notes-header wprm-block-text-bold wprm-align-left wprm-header-decoration-none\" style=\"\">Notes</h3><div class=\"wprm-spacer\" style=\"height: 15px;\"></div><div class=\"wprm-recipe-notes\"><table>\n<tr>\n<th>Nutrient</th>\n<th>Amount per Serving</th>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Calories</td>\n<td>300</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Fat</td>\n<td>20g</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Protein</td>\n<td>15g</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Carbs</td>\n<td>10g</td>\n</tr>\n</table></div></div>\n      <div class=\"wprm-spacer\" style=\"height: 40px;\"></div>\n      \n    </div>\n  </div>\n</div></div></div>\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"ingredients\"><strong>Ingredients</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Get ready to create a delicious Rotel Dip with these simple ingredients!</p>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image aligncenter size-full\"><img decoding=\"async\" width=\"400\" height=\"533\" src=\"/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/Fresh-Ingredients-for-ROTEL-DIP.webp\" alt=\"Fresh ingredients for ROTEL DIP displayed on a kitchen table.\" class=\"wp-image-5127\" srcset=\"/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/Fresh-Ingredients-for-ROTEL-DIP.webp 400w, /wp-content/uploads/2025/08/Fresh-Ingredients-for-ROTEL-DIP-225x300.webp 225w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 400px) 100vw, 400px\" /></figure>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li><strong>1 (10 oz) can Rotel diced tomatoes and green chilies</strong> – for a zesty base</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>1 lb <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Velveeta\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Velveeta cheese</a></strong> – cubed for smooth melting</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>1 lb ground beef</strong> – provides that hearty flavor</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>1 small onion</strong> – finely chopped for sweetness</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>2 cloves garlic</strong> – minced for a punch of flavor</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Optional: 1 tsp <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chili_powder\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">chili powder</a></strong> – for extra spice if desired</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Fresh cilantro or green onions</strong> – for garnish</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"how-to-make-rotel-dip\"><strong>How to Make ROTEL DIP</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Get ready to whip up a delicious ROTEL DIP in no time! With a preparation time of just 10 minutes and a cooking time of 15 minutes, you’ll have this cheesy delight ready to serve in about 25 minutes. Perfect for parties or a cozy night in!</p>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image aligncenter size-full\"><img decoding=\"async\" width=\"400\" height=\"533\" src=\"/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/Preparation-Steps-for-ROTEL-DIP.webp\" alt=\"Step-by-step preparation of ROTEL DIP, including browned beef, sautéed vegetables, melted cheese, and the final dish served with tortilla chips.\" class=\"wp-image-5128\" srcset=\"/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/Preparation-Steps-for-ROTEL-DIP.webp 400w, /wp-content/uploads/2025/08/Preparation-Steps-for-ROTEL-DIP-225x300.webp 225w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 400px) 100vw, 400px\" /></figure>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Step 1: Brown the Beef</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">In a skillet over medium heat, brown the ground beef until no longer pink. Drain any excess fat.</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Step 2: Sauté the Veggies</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Add chopped onion and minced garlic to the skillet. Sauté until softened, about 3–4 minutes.</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Step 3: Melt the Cheese</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Reduce heat to low. Add cubed Velveeta and the can of Rotel (undrained). Stir continuously until the cheese is fully melted and the mixture is smooth.</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Step 4: Season It Up</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Season with chili powder if desired. Stir to combine all the flavors.</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Step 5: Serve and Enjoy</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Transfer to a serving bowl. Garnish with cilantro or green onions. Serve warm with tortilla chips.</p>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"recipe-snapshot\"><strong>Recipe Snapshot</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-table\"><table class=\"has-fixed-layout\"><thead><tr><th>Feature</th><th>Details</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Category</td><td>Appetizer</td></tr><tr><td>Cuisine</td><td>American</td></tr><tr><td>Prep Time</td><td>10 minutes</td></tr><tr><td>Cook Time</td><td>15 minutes</td></tr><tr><td>Total Time</td><td>25 minutes</td></tr><tr><td>Dietary</td><td>Not specified</td></tr><tr><td>Serves</td><td>8</td></tr><tr><td>Best Served</td><td>Warm with tortilla chips</td></tr></tbody></table></figure>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"pro-tips-for-making-rotel-dip\"><strong>Pro Tips for Making ROTEL DIP</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Opt for a blend of cheeses for a richer flavor.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Use fresh jalapeños for a spicy kick.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Stir in some cream cheese for a creamier texture.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Serve with a variety of dippers like tortilla chips and veggies.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Make it ahead of time and reheat for easy entertaining.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"how-to-serve-this-rotel-dip\"><strong>How to Serve this ROTEL DIP</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Serve warm with crispy tortilla chips for the ultimate crunch.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Pair with fresh veggie sticks like carrots, celery, and bell peppers for a healthy twist.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Use as a zesty topping for baked potatoes or nachos.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Try it as a filling for quesadillas or tacos for a cheesy surprise.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"make-ahead-and-storage\"><strong>Make Ahead and Storage</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">You can easily prepare and store ROTEL DIP for later enjoyment:</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Storing ROTEL DIP Leftovers</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Allow the dip to cool to room temperature.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Transfer to an airtight container.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Store in the refrigerator for up to 3 days.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Freezing ROTEL DIP</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Let the dip cool completely before freezing.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Use a freezer-safe container or heavy-duty freezer bag.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Label with the date and freeze for up to 2 months.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Reheating ROTEL DIP</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Thaw in the refrigerator overnight if frozen.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Reheat in a saucepan over low heat, stirring frequently.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>For microwave, heat in short intervals, stirring in between.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Add a splash of milk for creaminess if needed.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Explore more easy <a href=\"https://www.grandmarecipe.com/category/breakfast/\"><strong>breakfast</strong></a> recipes, quick <a href=\"https://www.grandmarecipe.com/category/lunch/\"><strong>lunch</strong></a> ideas, cozy <a href=\"https://www.grandmarecipe.com/category/dinner/\"><strong>dinner</strong></a> meals, tasty <a href=\"https://www.grandmarecipe.com/category/snacks/\"><strong>snacks</strong></a>, and delightful <a href=\"https://www.grandmarecipe.com/category/dessert/\"><strong>dessert</strong></a>.</p>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"fa-qs\"><strong>FAQs</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Here’s a helpful FAQ about this recipe:</p>\n\n\n<div id=\"rank-math-faq\" class=\"rank-math-block\">\n<div class=\"rank-math-list \">\n<div id=\"faq-question-1\" class=\"rank-math-list-item\">\n<h3 class=\"rank-math-question \"><strong>1. What is Ro-Tel dip made of?</strong></h3>\n<div class=\"rank-math-answer \">\n\n<p>Ro-Tel dip is a delicious and creamy blend typically made with Ro-Tel tomatoes, cheese, and often cream cheese. The combination creates a rich, flavorful dip that’s perfect for parties or game day. You can also customize it by adding ingredients like ground beef or spices to suit your taste!</p>\n\n</div>\n</div>\n<div id=\"faq-question-2\" class=\"rank-math-list-item\">\n<h3 class=\"rank-math-question \"><strong>2. Why do people put cream cheese in Ro-Tel dip?</strong></h3>\n<div class=\"rank-math-answer \">\n\n<p>Cream cheese adds a wonderful creaminess and richness to Ro-Tel dip, balancing the acidity of the tomatoes and enhancing the overall flavor. It helps create a smooth texture that makes the dip perfect for scooping with chips or veggies!</p>\n\n</div>\n</div>\n<div id=\"faq-question-3\" class=\"rank-math-list-item\">\n<h3 class=\"rank-math-question \"><strong>3. Do I need cream cheese for Ro-Tel dip?</strong></h3>\n<div class=\"rank-math-answer \">\n\n<p>While cream cheese is a popular ingredient that adds creaminess, you can make Ro-Tel dip without it if you prefer a lighter version. You can substitute it with sour cream or a non-dairy alternative to achieve a similar texture and flavor. The dip will still be delicious!</p>\n\n</div>\n</div>\n<div id=\"faq-question-4\" class=\"rank-math-list-item\">\n<h3 class=\"rank-math-question \"><strong>4. Is Ro-Tel dip a southern thing?</strong></h3>\n<div class=\"rank-math-answer \">\n\n<p>Yes, Ro-Tel dip is often associated with Southern cuisine, particularly in Texas and surrounding states. It has become a beloved dish at gatherings and celebrations, showcasing the region&#8217;s love for bold flavors and hearty snacks. However, it has gained popularity across the country and is enjoyed by many!</p>\n\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"final-thoughts\"><strong>Final Thoughts</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Now that you have the scoop on making delicious Rotel Dip, it’s time to gather your friends and dive in! This creamy, zesty dip is perfect for game nights or cozy gatherings. Remember, it’s super simple and oh-so-rewarding. So grab those chips, and enjoy every cheesy bite—your taste buds will thank you!</p>\n",
